      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims a general meaning: that symptoms/patterns are “experienced as fitting with the person’s way of coping rather than feeling alien.” The provided packet does not define “ego-syntonic” in those terms; it only states that core eating-disorder psychopathology is “reinforcing and ego syntonic” in relation to treatment resistance.",
        "The definition links ego-syntonic features with resistance to treatment. While the packet does mention that ego syntonic is “resulting in resistance to treatment” (in the context of eating disorders), the claimed general experiential framing (“fitting… rather than feeling alien”) is not supported."
